<title>USA: Munich Re U.S. unit chief resigns.</title>
<headline>Munich Re U.S. unit chief resigns.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Re Corp, a unit of Germany-based Munich Re Group, said on Friday that Paul Inderbitzin resigned as chairman, president and chief executive officer to pursue personal business interests.</p>
<p>Inderbitzin has been succeeded as president and chief executive by Edward Noonan, president of American Re-Insurance Co's domestic insurance company operations since 1994, the company said.</p>
<p>Hans-Jorgen Schinzler, chairman of the board of management of Munich Reinsurance Co, has become chairman of the American Re's board, the company said.</p>
